# Jackson wiki

The user's own notes, verified on their lab and machines. Treat them as the first source for the
topics above; they hold paths, IDs, gotchas and fixes that are not on the web.

## Where it is

- Root: `C:/Users/Administrator/Documents/projects/LLMwiki` (git repo; older docs call it `C:\OneDrive\Jackson\`, which no longer exists).
- Entry point: `index.md` at the root - one line per page, grouped by domain.
- Sub-indexes: `APEX/index.md` for the APEX tree.
- This checkout holds the `APEX/`, `aHDS/` and `AGM-AGT/` folders. `index.md` also lists pages
  from the full vault that are not in this checkout (Wingman, PiKVM, Niagara, PAPI2, BIOS, AI tools
  and others). When a linked page is missing, say "listed in the wiki index but not on this machine"
  and use the one-line summary from the index only as a hint, not as fact.
- Pages are linked as `[[file-name]]` (no `.md`, no folder). Resolve one with
  `Glob` on `**/file-name.md` under the root.

## How to use it

1. Read `index.md` (about 180 lines) and pick the pages that match the task. If nothing fits,
   `Grep` the root for the key terms before concluding the wiki has nothing.
2. Read the matching pages in full and follow their `## 相关` links when they bear on the task.
3. Answer from them and cite the page path. Where a page is marked `draft`, says "unclear" or
   "not yet verified", or conflicts with what you observe now, say so; do not smooth it over.
4. If the wiki has nothing, say that plainly, then use other sources.
5. Shared PMM plugin skills (pmm-apex and others) cover some of the same topics. Check the wiki
   too and prefer it where they differ, since it records what happened on the user's own setup;
   name both sources when they disagree.

## Writing to it

Only when the user asks. Then follow the root `CLAUDE.md` / `WIKI-AGENTS.md`: standard
frontmatter, kebab-case file name, a `## 相关` block with 3-5 wikilinks, and a new line in
`index.md` under the right group.

