const hydHtml  = await page.content();              // after hydration

const strip = h => h
  .replace(/<script[\s\S]*?<\/script>/g, '')
  .replace(/<style[\s\S]*?<\/style>/g, '')
# 网站开发：响应式、移动端实用验收与复发学习

版本：1.3.0（2026-10-21 新增 §0 默认要求；2026-10-22 品位禁令改为 FAIL，Jobs review 铁律）。用户明确要求：2026-10-14，网站要重视响应式和移动端体验，降低理解与操作负担；agent 要实际打开使用，主动发现、解决问题，并对重复问题学习和预防。

适用：新建网站、修改网站 UI、修复网站问题。以本文件所在的 active harness 为来源，项目既有规则和当前任务授权共同限定范围。本文件定义当前网站体验验收；`ui-build-doctrine.md` 保留已有布局循环细节，`computer-use-acceptance.md` 提供通用启动、取证与有界修复流程。只更新规则文件时做规则加载验证，不据此声称某个网站体验通过。

## 0. Default requirements, even when unasked

User direction (2026-10-21): "很多时候没提移动端网页，agent 就默认只优化 PC 端网页，这是不对的要响应式的，
移动端的体验，交互，界面，速度等等，SEO 等等都十分重要，这些都是默认的要求". A request to build or change a
website that never mentions phones, speed or SEO still requires all of the following. Only the
user's own words waive one (for example "desktop-only admin tool"); "not requested" is not a
waiver. The list is `routes/web-defaults.md`; the `web` module of `core/policy.json` points every
agent to it without the user naming a site (`context_modules`, docs/adr/0034): on each session whose
directory is a web project (an `index.html`, or a front-end framework in `package.json`), at the first
edit of a front-end file (`.tsx`, `.vue`, `.css`, `.html` ...; harness and temp-folder report pages
excepted), and on prompts that name a site, a page, its UI or its users' experience.

**Steal, then let the user choose** (user, 2026-10-29: "我现在发现 agent 给我建网站，自己瞎搞，good artists copy great
artist steal，要找对标，然后给我几个让我选，效果要部署到线上，有时候我是手机上远程的，不在电脑旁边"). A new site, a redesign or a
new interaction or visual direction is never improvised, and its look is the user's choice (RULES.md "Benchmark gate"):

1. Find the benchmarks: the best sites for the same job and buyer (category leaders, sites the buyer already pays, products the
   user named), at least two, opened and captured, not recalled. `find-demand` and `website-mvp` find rivals; a gallery of
   well-made sites helps only when they do the same job.
2. Build 2 to 4 options, each stealing from one named benchmark: its look, layout and interaction patterns (type scale, colour,
   density, hero structure, how the core action works). Never its words, images, logos or brand; the features and the value are
   ours. The options differ in direction, not in shades of one direction. Each is a real, working first screen and core page.
3. Put every option online: a static build (`index.html` at its root) is deployed by the tool to its own Cloudflare Pages project;
   a server app uses its host's preview deploy and passes the `url`. Deploy is grant G1; a localhost link or a screenshot alone is
   not an option. A deploy that fails after two routes is `BLOCKED — <exact error>`.
4. Send one phone page: `python <harness>/scripts/design_options.py --spec options.json` checks each link answers over public
   HTTPS, captures each option next to its benchmark at phone width, adds your pick and why, publishes the page with
   `share_page.py` and prints `phone_url` and the card line. Put both in the reply with one line: reply A, B or C.
5. Do not wait idle and do not pick for the user: until they answer, build only what no option changes (data, backend, SEO, the
   core flow's logic, tests), then stop with the question. The chosen option becomes the benchmark the Jobs review compares against.

Scope: a new site or a new direction. A bug fix, copy change or small change inside an already chosen look needs none of this.

**Value first: the goal of every site** (user, 2026-10-28: "我创建网站追求的是价值感，就是给用户创造额外的价值，
我才能够收到钱。目标就是为用户创造价值，而且在创造价值的不同阶段可能有不同的答案，要不断地去追问这些"). A site earns
money only by giving its buyer clearly more value than the price, and the buyer must *see* that value without
reading: real outputs, the product in use and the scenario as pictures, not paragraphs ("用户也没耐心看文字").
Sell the buyer's result, not the mechanism (Skillify, 2026-10-28: the buyer saw "installs skills for an agent"
and felt no value; the value was the launch video, page and deck those skills produce). The answers change as
the product moves on, so ask these again at every stage, write the current answers in the plan or report, and
let real data replace guesses as soon as there is any:

| Stage | Questions to answer before moving on |
|---|---|
| Before building | Who pays, for which result? What does that result cost them today (money, hours, a hire)? Is the buyer also the user, or does someone or something else (an agent, a team) use it, and what does the buyer get? Why is it worth more than the price? |
| While building | Does the first session end with a real result the buyer would use as it is? How many steps and minutes until then? What can be cut without losing value? |
| Before launch | Without reading, does a stranger see the real result in 5 seconds (real outputs and the scenario as pictures, not mockups or text)? Which claim is still words where a real output could show it? Is every value claim true and reproducible? |
| After launch | What do the numbers say users actually got (results made, repeat use, payment, refunds, feedback)? Where do they stop before reaching value? What is the next value worth paying for, and when do they meet it? |

| Area | Default | Measured by `scripts/web-check.py` |
|---|---|---|
| Responsive layout | Mobile-first: design and build at 375 px, then tablet and desktop; viewport meta with `width=device-width`; fluid grids; images, tables and code fit or scroll locally | viewport meta, no sideways scroll at 375 px and 1440 px (FAIL); text cut off by hidden overflow (WARN) |
| Touch interaction | Targets 44 px as the design goal, never under 24 px when crowded; no hover-only action; inputs at 16 px or more with the right `type`, `inputmode` and `autocomplete` | WCAG 2.5.8 target size (FAIL); under 44 px and inputs under 16 px (WARN) |
| Phone interface | 16 px body text; one clear main action per screen; navigation reachable with one thumb; loading, empty, error and success states visible; nothing fixed covers content or the main button | typical text size, text under 12 px, fixed layers covering over 30% of the first screen (WARN) |
| Speed | Mid-range phone on 4G: LCP 2.5 s or less, CLS 0.1 or less, TBT 200 ms or less; little JavaScript; images sized, compressed (AVIF/WebP), lazy below the fold, with width and height | LCP measured after the first byte (FAIL > 3.5 s, the Core Web Vitals poor line less a typical first byte) and CLS (FAIL > 0.25); first byte, TBT, page weight and JS bytes (WARN: lab proxies that vary with this host's network and CPU); oversized, eager and unsized images (WARN) |
| Taste | The user's design bar below (readable, no gradient text, no emoji icons, one language per page, product shown working); a Jobs review that ends satisfied (iron law) | text under WCAG AA contrast, gradient-filled text, emoji icons, a second language on the page or `lang` not matching the text (FAIL); on landing pages no product visual, repeated "heading + cards" grids, empty-slogan H1, text failing only against a gradient's average (WARN) |
| SEO | Unique title (10-65 chars) and meta description (50-170); one H1; `lang`; canonical; Open Graph; JSON-LD where it fits; robots.txt and sitemap; indexable (user preference: ship indexable) | missing title, description, H1, noindex or robots.txt blocking all (FAIL); the rest (WARN) |
| Core task (2026-10-28: "用户核心使用步骤要非常短，核心操作也必须在一个页面完成，就连下滑也不用就可以完成核心功能操作") | Fewest steps, one page, and at phone size the core action starts and finishes in the first screen without scrolling | no field or call to action in the first 375x812 screen, or a form begun there submitting from below it (FAIL; legal, docs, blog and pricing pages exempt) |
| GEO (2026-10-28) | Content in the served HTML (AI crawlers mostly run no JavaScript); robots.txt admits search and AI crawlers; `/llms.txt`; plain, quotable answers (skill `geo-page`) | H1 missing from the served HTML, robots.txt shutting out GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot and the like (FAIL); no llms.txt (WARN) |
| Agents and accessibility (2026-10-28) | Agents act through the accessibility tree: named, real controls; visible field labels; `<main>`; keyboard with a visible focus ring; `prefers-reduced-motion` honoured; the core task reachable by URL or a plain form | unnamed controls (FAIL); placeholder-only labels, clickable non-controls, no `<main>`, no focus ring on the first Tab stop, endless animation under reduced motion (WARN) |
| Security (2026-10-29: "网站的安全也要关注") | HTTPS only; secrets only on the server (publishable keys excepted); server-side input validation and authorisation on every route; rate limits and bot checks on free or costly routes (`abuse-guard`); verified payment webhooks (`payment-integrity`); security headers; Secure, HttpOnly cookies; no served `.env`/`.git`; dependency audit and `launch-readiness` (plus `/security-review` in Claude Code) before go-live | plain HTTP off localhost, mixed content, secret keys in same-origin or inline JavaScript, an `.env` or `.git` served by content (FAIL); missing HSTS, CSP, nosniff or Referrer-Policy, cookies without Secure or HttpOnly, on HTTPS (WARN) |
| Analytics (2026-10-28) | PostHog alone (page views and the money events), loaded after render; GA4 only beside Google Ads, Clarity only past PostHog's replay quota | more than one tracker, or none on a public page (WARN) |

