usage: web-check.py [-h] [--out OUT] [--app] [--allow-noindex]
                    [--storage-state STORAGE_STATE]
                    url [url ...]

Measure a website's default requirements: mobile-first layout, touch, speed,
SEO and the measurable part of the user's design taste: readable contrast, no
gradient text, no emoji icons and one language per page (FAIL: the user's
explicit bans), and on landing pages a product visual, no repeated "heading +
cards" grids and no empty-slogan H1 (WARN). The user's site constraints
(2026-10-28) add the core task in the first phone screen, GEO (served HTML, AI
crawlers, llms.txt), accessibility that also lets agents use the page, and one
analytics tool.

positional arguments:
  url                   every page the change touched

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --out OUT             report folder (default ./.web-check)
  --app                 pages behind sign-in: skip search checks
  --allow-noindex       the user chose to keep this site out of search
                        (staging, private tool)
  --storage-state STORAGE_STATE
                        Playwright storage-state JSON for signed-in pages

