# Philosophy audit, round 4

Content verdict: no blocker or major found; two minor Sources defects remain. This is the content subreview, not the overall product verdict.

Reviewed HEAD `bc535e1ab91f33fdc2a5f3e3eb7724eaddad51bf`. All 45 catalog quotations, their glosses and limits, all 22 session descriptions, and every authored field in all 111 rounds/levels were read again. The per-ID record is `coverage.json`; the current extraction is `current-content.json`.

## Previous findings

- **R3-1: fixed in the revised content.** `h1-0` supplies an ordinary optician test and consultation about words while other resources remain fixed. It then explicitly asks the learner to doubt every checking resource simultaneously. Completion no longer depends on finding a self-loop. OC §§115, 341–345 support this distinction; §349 permits the local eyesight context. The authored point and game description were updated. Root owns the fresh phone/desktop journey and saved Notebook checks.
- **R3-2: fixed in the authored data.** Sign language now includes `written`, at `src/games/family/rounds.ts:88`. The early-games reviewer owns the fresh served-build chain check.

## P1 — minor — The Sources bibliography excludes a part it actually quotes

Where: http://localhost:3417/sources, `#w-PI` and `#pi-ppf-118`; `src/app/sources/page.tsx:14`; `src/content/sources.ts:229`. Fresh screenshots: `phone-pi-bibliography.png`, `desktop-pi-bibliography.png`, `phone-pi-ppf-118.png`, and `desktop-pi-ppf-118.png` in this directory.

The introductory bibliography labels the Anscombe quotations as Part I, but the aspect-seeing excerpt is from Part II, xi. The individual card correctly says Part II and gives the later PPF numbering; the group bibliography should agree. This is not a quotation wording error.

Concrete fix: change the bibliography to Parts I and II, retaining the individual Part II/PPF cross-reference.

## P2 — minor — Ranged references are sorted as concatenated numbers

Where: http://localhost:3417/sources, Investigations list; `src/app/sources/page.tsx:23`. Fresh evidence: `phone-pi-ppf-118.png` and `desktop-pi-ppf-118.png`; `live-sources.json` retains the served text order.

The list places §§19–20 after §293 and §§201–202 after Part II. The comparator deletes punctuation and concatenates the endpoints, treating these ranges as 1920 and 201202. This makes the promised reference page harder to navigate in section order.

Concrete fix: extract the first section number for Part I and explicitly place Part II after Part I, instead of deleting all nonnumeric characters.

## Primary comparison and limits of interpretation

The primary editions were reopened via web browsing during this review. Full-text comparisons used the stable copies already retained in `../../codex-review-r3/philosophy/`; SHA-256 hashes are recorded in `coverage.json`.

- [Tractatus, 1922 Ogden edition](https://www.wittgensteinproject.org/w/index.php/Tractatus_Logico-Philosophicus_(English)).
- [Investigations, Anscombe English scan](https://static1.squarespace.com/static/54889e73e4b0a2c1f9891289/t/564b61a4e4b04eca59c4d232/1447780772744/Ludwig.Wittgenstein.-.Philosophical.Investigations.pdf).
- [On Certainty, Paul and Anscombe, 1969](https://www.circuitdebater.org/circuitdebater/archive/w/file/view/On%20Certainty.pdf/507953768/On%20Certainty.pdf).


