# Late-game review evidence

R3-1 status: partly. The fresh-user activity is fixed; a minor saved-progress migration gap remains. There are no newly observed blocker/major runtime findings in this review scope.

## Minor: obsolete certainty completion survives the corrected exercise

Where: http://localhost:3417/play/hinges, h1-0; http://localhost:3417/notebook; `src/games/hinges/rounds.ts:16`, `src/lib/progress.ts:175`, `src/components/notebook.tsx:81`.

Load the genuine prior review save from `qa/codex-review-r3/late-games/phone/storage.json` or the desktop equivalent in the current build. Enter Hinges: the previous end card is retained. Expand the Doubt it answers in Notebook: it displays the new contextual-check explanation, but still certifies the old results `Stands fast: My eyes are working.` and `Stands fast: Words like ...` as Right first time. The user is not asked to play the replacement exercise. Selecting Sessions → Doubt it manually opens the new exercise, so this is a migration defect, not a fresh-user failure.

Fix: version or replace the changed h1-0 activity identifier and invalidate only its obsolete completion/draft. Resume the revised exercise for these saves while preserving unrelated progress. Ensure the old earned answer is not presented as evidence that the new distinction was learned.

Evidence: `migration.py`, `migration.json`, `phone-migration/returning-entry.png`, `phone-migration/returning-notebook.png`; desktop equivalents. The saved state is loaded verbatim, with no invented completion data.

## Fresh-user R3-1 evidence

`python -B -X utf8 qa/codex-review-r4/late-games/recheck.py` operated the local eyesight test, persisted it through reload, checked word meaning separately, and explicitly doubted all checking resources on phone and desktop. The activity no longer awards hinge status for finding a circular graph. `recheck.json` and both device-recheck folders retain text, storage, and screenshots.

## Coverage

- `review.py`: all 20 current late-game rounds completed on each device: pupil r-1–r-4, beetle bb1-0/bb1-1/bb1-3/bb1-5, diary bb2-0/bb2-3/bb2-4, hinges h1-0/h1-3/h1-4/h1-4b/h1-5/h2-0/h2-1/h2-2/h2-5. All 6 sessions chosen through Sessions navigation. Wrong choices exercised in all three games. 88 screenshots per device. No collected page errors, console errors, or horizontal overflow. `coverage.json`, `observations.json`, and phone/desktop storage files hold the actual results.
- `edges.py`: both devices retained partial diary choices and predictions after reload, rendered 0/5 calibration and 0/3 prediction corrections, retained a wrong pupil answer on reload, retained local eye-check draft, and opened the revised pupil syllabus from genuine round-1 storage.
- `end_checks.py`: final end cards for pupil, beetle and hinges linked to the correct next idea and replayed; expanded Signposts sources included PI §198 and §202.
- Design: the paper palette, serif hierarchy, vermilion actions, illustrated scenes, progress line, and idea cards persist through all inspected game states and end cards. No broken image, overlapping control, horizontal clipping, or new layout defect was observed. All 176 primary captures and 38 edge captures were inspected through contact sheets, with full-resolution views for changed certainty content. Additional recheck/migration captures were inspected through extra sheets; expanded Notebook text was also read from recorded DOM text.
- The activities concern rule-following, private sensation criteria, and the dependence of checking on things held fixed. No English-course objective or language-skill score appeared in these journeys. Source accuracy is owned by the separate philosophy audit.

No product files were edited and no server was started, stopped, or rebuilt. All browser contexts launched here were closed.

Not covered: physical touch hardware; Safari/Firefox; screen-reader speech; complete keyboard-only journeys; all sorting/check-path permutations; a measured learning-retention study. Root owns the overall /sources, /notebook, home, accessibility audit, and combined all-games-complete state.

